<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unstrut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Unstrut is a river of about 190 kilometres in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a>. On its banks the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> crushed the Thuringian kingdom in 531, and Henry IV defeated the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> there in 1075. Its lower valley is part of the Saale-Unstrut wine region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unstrut.jpg" alt="Unstrut" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mazbln · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unstrut_Bruecke_Weischuetz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
